                                "sense_id": "c121ef7c-18a5-3609-bb4b-51101ef72166",
                                "text": "a washerwoman, who exposes hard-bake for sale in her parlor-window"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "390fcc2d-4188-4448-9cd5-7f269a4d465a",
                                "sense_id": "c121ef7c-18a5-3609-bb4b-51101ef72166",
                                "text": "They both had a taste for painting theatrical characters; for hard bake and raspberry tarts; for sliding and skating in the Regent's Park and the Serpentine, when the weather permitted; for going to the play, whither they were often conducted, by Mr. Osborne's orders, by Rowson, Master George's appointed body-servant, with whom they sat in great comfort in the pit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e239485-d329-4d6c-b392-ae5303221e5d",
                                "sense_id": "c121ef7c-18a5-3609-bb4b-51101ef72166",
                                "text": "Harmless improving books were provided for the crew to read, and vanilla ices, sugar-plums, hardbake and raspberry jam were served out every day with a liberal hand."
                            }
